dict(pas="3.2", w="三/the three | 家=jiā/families, houses | 者/(topic: 'as for…') | 以《/with, to the strains of | 雍》=yōng/the Yong — an ode of the Zhou royal temple | 徹。=chè/cleared away (the sacrificial vessels) | ^子/the Master | 曰：「『/said | 相=xiàng/assisting, attending — Zhu Xi: 助也 | 維=wéi/are (copula particle) | 辟=bì/the princes — the feudal lords | 公，/(and) dukes | ^天子=tiān zǐ/the Son of Heaven — the Zhou king//Heaven//son | 穆穆』，=mù mù/solemn and grave, deep and still | ^奚/what | 取=qǔ/is taken (from it) | 於/in | 三/the three | 家=jiā/families' | 之/'s | 堂？」=táng/hall",
  l="The Three Families cleared away to the Yong.\nThe Master said: “‘The helpers are the princes and dukes;\nthe Son of Heaven, solemn and still’ —\nwhat of this is taken up in the halls of the Three Families?”",
  i="The Three Families had the Yong sung as the sacrificial vessels were cleared away. The Master said: “‘The princes and dukes attend him; the Son of Heaven stands solemn and grave’ — what in these words has any place in the halls of the Three Families?”",
  n="三家 are the three great families of Lu, Mengsun, Shusun and Jisun; 者 after them marks the topic. 雍 is the ode 雝 in the Zhou temple hymns (Odes 282), sung when the vessels were cleared after the king's ancestral sacrifice; 徹 chè is 'to clear away'. The Master answers by quoting two of its lines. 相 is read xiàng, 'to assist' (Zhu Xi: 相去聲…助也), not xiāng 'mutually'. 維 is a copula particle common in the Odes, 'are'. 辟 is bì, 'lord, prince': Zhu Xi takes 辟公 as the feudal lords; He Yan's Bao Xian says the lords and the heirs of the two earlier royal houses, who came to help at the king's sacrifice. 穆穆 is the doubled adjective of the king's bearing, 'deep and remote'. 奚取 'what is taken?': in a grandee's hall there are no assisting princes and no Son of Heaven, so the words mean nothing there — Zhu Xi says the Master mocks their ignorant presumption. Zhu Xi quotes Master Cheng: Lu itself was wrongly granted the king's rites and music for the Duke of Zhou's merit, and the families copied their own lord."),
